{"full":"hf:aminediroHF/trainer-generator-bf16-mismatch","spaceId":"aminediroHF/trainer-generator-bf16-mismatch","name":"Defeating the trainer-generator precision mismatch in TRL","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","reinforcement-learning","numerical-precision","GRPO","PPO","training","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":19,"created":"2026-04-01T12:15:13.000Z","updated":"2026-04-18T13:35:10.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://aminedirohf-trainer-generator-bf16-mismatch.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/aminediroHF/trainer-generator-bf16-mismatch","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T17:10:46.994Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T17:10:46.994Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T17:10:46.994Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🎯","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Phantom PPO clipping from numerical precision gaps prevents RL convergence.","We show that async GRPO training fails when the training forward pass (FP32) and the vLLM inference server (BF16) use different numerical precision. The root cause is a precision gap that triggers phantom PPO clipping, zeroing out gradient signal for tokens whose policy has not actually changed.","This repository hosts the interactive research article Defeating the trainer-generator precision mismatch in TRL, by Amine Dirhoussi, Quentin Gallouédec, Edward Beeching, Lewis Tunstall, Kashif Rasul, and Leandro von Werra (Hugging Face)."],"features":["BF16 arithmetic and where precision loss originates","The GRPO loss and the role of the importance sampling ratio","How small logit errors amplify into large policy ratio deviations","Phantom clipping and gradient corruption in async rollouts","Interventions that restore convergence"],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/aminediroHF/trainer-generator-bf16-mismatch/blob/main/READM